{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If your brother, your mother's son, entices you.</b> For he is beloved thus, for you both emerged from one womb, but the father's sons are not so beloved to one another. And furthermore, their way is to hate one another because of the inheritance." "<b>In secret, saying.</b> Scripture speaks of the usual case, for the way of such an ugly matter is to be spoken in secret. And the Rav Bekhor Shor says: since it is said ״הולך רכיל מגלה סוד״, do not say that because he spoke to you in secret it is forbidden to reveal his secret — for on the contrary, do not cover for him, for it is forbidden to cover his words."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:54.427802244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}